# .chief/config — Chief project configuration (sourced as bash by the engine).
# Uncomment/edit to override the defaults shown.

CHIEF_PROVIDER=claude            # AI provider: claude | devin | opencode | amp
# CHIEF_MODEL=                    # optional provider-specific model override (not amp: it has
#                                # no model selector, so --model is refused for it)
# CHIEF_TOOL=claude               # legacy alias; use CHIEF_PROVIDER instead
# CHIEF_BASE_BRANCH=main          # integration branch
# CHIEF_TASKS_DIR=tasks/chief    # where tasklist JSONs live (+ completed/)
# CHIEF_STATE_DIR=.chief/state   # gitignored per-run runtime state
# CHIEF_VERIFY=.chief/verify.sh  # branch verification hook (exit 0 = pass; empty = skip)
# CHIEF_AGENT_CONTEXT=.chief/agent-context.md   # project-specific agent instructions
# CHIEF_AUTO_MERGE=1             # 1 = verify+merge completed branches; 0 = leave for review
# --- cost-avoidance preset (docs/guides/local-inference-preset.md) -------------------
# CHIEF_PRESET=local             # one switch: run every agent turn on a LOCAL/self-hosted
#                                # endpoint via opencode — zero API cost, lower coding quality
# CHIEF_LOCAL_ENDPOINT=          # required by the preset: base URL of your local OpenAI-compatible
#                                # server, e.g. http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
# CHIEF_LOCAL_MODEL=             # required by the preset: model id to ask it for (chief models opencode)
# CHIEF_LOCAL_ENDPOINT_ENV=OPENAI_BASE_URL   # env var the endpoint is published as
# CHIEF_LOCAL_API_KEY=local                  # placeholder credential local servers accept
# CHIEF_LOCAL_API_KEY_ENV=OPENAI_API_KEY     # env var that credential is published as
# --- the per-story DIFF-SIZE BUDGET (docs/reference/diff-budget.md) -----------------
# Larger diffs carry higher conflict probability, so change size is the lever. Chief
# measures every branch's diff against the base, DECOMPOSED BY STORY, and reports any
# story that went over. Defaults shown; unset means exactly these.
# CHIEF_DIFF_BUDGET=warn         # warn = report and merge anyway (default) · block =
#                                # hold the branch for `chief approve`, like an overlap
#                                # zone · off = do not measure at all
# CHIEF_DIFF_BUDGET_LINES=400    # changed lines (added+deleted) per story; 0 disables
# CHIEF_DIFF_BUDGET_FILES=20     # changed files per story;                 0 disables
# --- the OPT-IN batch MERGE QUEUE (docs/explanation/drivers-and-safety.md) ----------
# OFF by default, and off is the serialized floor: rebase -> re-verify -> --no-ff, one
# tasklist at a time, which is chief's correctness guarantee. Set N > 1 to batch up to
# N merge-ready branches, stack them on the base and verify the batch TIP ONCE instead
# of paying the verify gate once per branch. Merges stay --no-ff, one commit per
# tasklist, serialized against the base; only the VERIFICATION is amortized. Needs
# `chief run -p N` with N > 1 to have anything to batch. `chief run --merge-batch[=N]`
# sets it for one run and beats this file.
# CHIEF_MERGE_BATCH=1            # 1 = off (the floor) · N = max branches per batch
# CHIEF_MERGE_BATCH_WAIT=120     # seconds a batch leader waits for peers; 0 = never wait
